# Two-File GitFlow Deployment Pipeline

## What Changes

Replace `deploy-pipeline.yml` with **two separate workflow files**, each triggered
by a Git event — no manual button needed.

| File | Trigger | Environment |
|---|---|---|
| `deploy-qa.yml` | Push to `feature/**`, `fix/**`, `bugfix/**`, `hotfix/**`, `chore/**` | `qa` |
| `deploy-prod.yml` | Push to `main` (i.e. when a PR is merged) | `production` |

`ci.yml` stays unchanged.

---

## Full Flow

```
Developer pushes to feature branch
        │
        ▼
  deploy-qa.yml runs automatically
  ┌──────────────────────────────┐
  │ Job 1: pre-deploy            │  quality gates + pytest
  │ Job 2: deploy-qa             │  deploy to QA  (environment: qa)
  │ Job 3: post-deploy-qa        │  gates + smoke tests on QA
  └──────────────────────────────┘
        │  QA looks good
        ▼
  Developer opens PR → main
        │
        ▼
  ci.yml runs on the PR (existing behaviour)
        │
        ▼
  PR reviewed & merged to main
        │
        ▼
  deploy-prod.yml runs automatically
  ┌──────────────────────────────┐
  │ Job 1: pre-deploy            │  quality gates + pytest
  │ Job 2: deploy-prod           │  deploy to Production
  │                              │  (environment: production)
  │                              │  ← approval gate if Required Reviewers set
  │ Job 3: post-deploy-prod      │  gates + smoke tests on Production
  └──────────────────────────────┘
        │
        ▼
     🏁 Done
```

